<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!--
      The demo flavour strips network permissions that arrive from dependencies.

      WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Our own manifests declare no INTERNET permission, but the merged
      manifest had one anyway: com.google.android.datatransport:transport-backend-cct, a Google
      telemetry uploader pulled in transitively by ML Kit, declares INTERNET and
      ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE. Nothing in our source would have shown that. It was caught by
      verifyDemoDebugHasNoInternet reading the MERGED manifest, which is why that check reads the
      merged result rather than our sources.

      Removing the permission is the guarantee. A library that has no INTERNET permission cannot
      reach the network whatever it tries to do, so the airplane-mode claim in spec 14.4 holds even
      with the telemetry code still linked in.

      Do not "fix" a future merge conflict by deleting these lines. If a dependency needs INTERNET,
      it does not belong in the demo build.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" tools:node="remove" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" tools:node="remove" />

</manifest>
